Wait for hs2 to have the power-levels change before charlie's local join (NoCreators race).

Tests: TestRestrictedRoomsLocalJoinNoCreatorsUsesPowerLevelsV11, ...V12,
TestKnockRestrictedRoomsLocalJoinNoCreatorsUsesPowerLevelsV11, ...V12 (all four share
doTestRestrictedRoomsLocalJoinNoCreatorsUsesPowerLevels).

Alice (hs1) gives bob (hs2) invite power with SendEventSynced, which waits for the event on
hs1 only. The test then has charlie join through hs2 straight away, and hs2 can only
authorise that join through bob once the power-levels event has arrived over federation.
On a loaded host it had not: charlie's join was refused 15 ms after hs1 accepted the
change (docs/status/14-test-and-conformance.md, session 6), and all four failed in four
runs of 2026-09-30 and on c2d74174. The patch makes bob sync until he sees the event,
which is the precondition the assertion depends on; the assertion itself is unchanged.
Applied by tests/complement/apply_patches.sh. Upstream: matrix-org/complement
tests/restricted_rooms_test.go (Apache-2.0).

